Now I understand the boot seam. The fix for the BLOCKING boot-sweep race:

- `_initializeSession()` calls `_retentionBootCheck()` BEFORE resolving `config.sessionName` via `_sessionNameMatches`.
- Fix: resolve the resume target first (when `config.sessionName` is set), then pass the matched id as `currentSessionId` to the sweper.

But careful about the ordering: `_retentionBootCheck()` also must run before `unawaited(_sweepHeaderOnlySessions())`? Actually the header-only sweep is separate. The cleanest restructure:

```dart
Future<Session> _initializeSession() async {
 final name = config.sessionName?.trim();
 List<SessionMetadata> matches = const [];
 SessionMetadata? resolved;
 if (name != null && name.isNotEmpty) {
   matches = await _sessionNameMatches(name);
   resolved = _resolveSessionNameMatch(matches, onAmbiguous: ...);
 }
 await _retentionBootCheck(currentSessionId: resolved?.id);
 ...
}
``

Wait — but resolving the name match before the sweep is precisely what the reviewer suggested: "resolve the resume target before sweeping and pass it as currentSessionId (or exempt it explicitly), e.g. resolve config.sessionName via _sessionNameMatches first and hand the sweper the match id; only then run enforceAtBoot()."

So restructure `_initializeSession`:

```dart
Future<Session> _initializeSession() async {
 // Resolve the resume target BEFORE the retention sweep: the sweper
 // must exempt the session this process is about to open — its
 // presence row registers only after the load, so at sweep time the
 // id is the only protection (gh-1746 review: boot-sweep data-loss race).
 final name = config.sessionName?.trim();
 List<SessionMetadata> matches = const [];
 SessionMetadata? metadata;
 if (name != null && name.isNotEmpty) {
   matches = await _sessionNameMatches(name);
   metadata = _resolveSessionNameMatch(
     matches,
     onAmbiguous: (all) {
       _startupAmbiguousSessions = all;
       _startupAmbiguousName = name;
     },
   );
 }
 await _retentionBootCheck(currentSessionId: metadata?.id);
 unawaited(_sweepHeaderOnlySessions());
 if (name != null && name.isNotEmpty) {
   if (metadata != null) {
     ... return _loadSession(metadata);
   }
   return _createSession(name: name);
 }
 return _createSession();
}
``

And `_retentionBootCheck({String? currentSessionId})` passes `currentSessionId: currentSessionId` to the sweper.

Edge: onAmbiguous fires when matches.length > 1 and no single local — it auto-resolves (picks most recent). The metadata returned is non-null in that case. Also, note that when ambiguous, `_startupAmbiguousSessions` is set — same as before. Good.

Now also: what about `keepNamed: false` resume by name (a named session)? Resolved metadata covers that too — the resume target is exempted regardless of keepNamed. 

