``

Wait — but resolving the name match before the sweep is precisely what the reviewer suggested: "resolve the resume target before sweeping and pass it as currentSessionId (or exempt it explicitly), e.g. resolve config.sessionName via _sessionNameMatches first and hand the sweper the match id; only then run enforceAtBoot()."

So restructure `_initializeSession`:

```dart
Future<Session> _initializeSession() async {
 // Resolve the resume target BEFORE the retention sweep: the sweper
 // must exempt the session this process is about to open — its
 // presence row registers only after the load, so at sweep time the
 // id is the only protection (gh-1746 review: boot-sweep data-loss race).
 final name = config.sessionName?.trim();
 List<SessionMetadata> matches = const [];
 SessionMetadata? metadata;
 if (name != null && name.isNotEmpty) {
   matches = await _sessionNameMatches(name);
   metadata = _resolveSessionNameMatch(
     matches,
     onAmbiguous: (all) {
       _startupAmbiguousSessions = all;
       _startupAmbiguousName = name;
     },
   );
