Wait, "walk blockers largest-first until held > remaining - cap": accumulate until the held sum EXCEEDS the overflow — those sessions ALONE prove the cap cannot be met. With overflow 430: first candidate 900 → held=900 > 430 → stop → [900]. 

But careful with the LOOP semantics: add first, then check. Edge: overflow exactly met (held == overflow)? Then remaining - cap could be brought to 0 IF those were deletable — but they're exempt, so the honest minimal set is held >= overflow. Let me use: stop when held >= overflow (after adding). Edge: overflow == 0? Can't be — remaining > cap means overflow ≥ 1.

Edge: what if exempt sessions' total < overflow? Impossible — remaining = total - freed and all non-deleted are exempt... held(max) = sum of all non-deleted = remaining... wait remaining includes deleted-freed... hmm: remaining = usage.totalBytes - freed where freed = deleted bytes. So remaining = sum of non-deleted units. overflow = remaining - cap > 0. Sum of all non-deleted = remaining > overflow. So the walk always terminates with held >= overflow. ✓

